<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria M1 rises 10.56 pct, M2 up 6.02 pct in wee.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria M1 rises 10.56 pct, M2 up 6.02 pct in wee.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian M1 money supply rose to 982.8 billion levs on July 4 from 888.8 billion levs a week earlier and M2 increased to 4,030.4 billion levs from 3,801.5 billion levs, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Total broad money rose 6.26 percent to 4,269.5 billion levs in the week to July 4.</p>
<p>Conversion of foreign currency-denominated deposits into levs was made at the central bank fixings of 1,000 levs per mark on July 4, 990.6 for June 27 and 921.5 for May 30.</p>
<p>The lev was pegged at 1,000 per mark under an IMF-prescribed fixed exchange rate mechanism, known as currency board, launched on July 1.</p>
<p>The currency board system requires that levs in circulation should be fully matched by the central bank's foreign exchange reserves.</p>
